            <ArticleTitle>[Benzylpenicillin-induced leucopenia in subacute bacterial endocarditis (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>177-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the high-dose benzylpenicillin treatment of subacute bacterial endocarditis leucopenia can develop in rare cases. Often it is paralleled by anemia, sometimes also by a decrease in the number of platelets. Myalgia, gastric discomfort, or a sore threat deserve interest as premonitory symptoms. In every case this treatment inevitably needs through hematologic control.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
